# Financial Math — BigDecimal Only

All financial calculations MUST use `BigDecimal`. No `double` or `float` for money.

## SPEC-BINDING Values (NFR-1.2)
- CURRENCY_SCALE = 2, RATE_SCALE = 6
- Rounding = ROUND_HALF_UP (RoundingMode.HALF_UP)

## Rules

- ❌ `double amount = 100.50;`
- ✅ `BigDecimal amount = new BigDecimal("100.50");`

- ❌ `new BigDecimal(0.1)` — creates 0.1000000000000000055511...
- ✅ `new BigDecimal("0.1")` — exact

- ❌ `a.divide(b)` — throws ArithmeticException on non-terminating decimals
- ✅ `a.divide(b, 2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP)`

- Never compare with `==`. Use `.compareTo(BigDecimal.ZERO) > 0`
- Currency display: `.toPlainString()` not `.toString()` (avoids scientific notation)
